 "notes": [
  "GitHub fine-grained PATs DO support gists: docs.github.com/en/rest/gists/gists states that 'Create a gist' and 'Update a gist' work with fine-grained personal access tokens and require the \"Gists\" user permissions (write). The managing-your-personal-access-tokens page lists Gists (write) under Account permissions, noting account permissions apply only when the current user is the resource owner. Sources: https://docs.github.com/en/rest/gists/gists and https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/managing-your-personal-access-tokens . The permissions reference page has a 'User permissions for \"Gists\"' section (seen in its TOC) but its body was not readable via fetch.",
  "ROS 2 Lyrical Luth was released on May 22, 2026 (ROS Discourse announcement). It is an LTS release supported until May 2031. Tier 1: Ubuntu 26.04 (Resolute) amd64/arm64 and Windows 11; Tier 2: RHEL 10; Tier 3: Ubuntu 24.04 Noble, macOS, Debian Trixie, OpenEmbedded. docs.ros.org/en/lyrical/ exists (seen in search results) but docs.ros.org blocks direct fetches (Anubis bot protection), so docs.ros.org URLs are search-result verified. Jazzy (LTS) targets Ubuntu 24.04.",
  "Ubuntu Desktop download page currently offers Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS (Resolute Raccoon).",
  "cs50.harvard.edu week pages 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 9 returned server errors on fetch (rate limiting); each was verified via a search result with matching title.",
  "probabilistic-robotics.org disallows robot fetching and never appeared in search results; used Thrun's Stanford page robots.stanford.edu/probabilistic-robotics/ instead.",
  "Practical Electronics for Inventors: no official publisher page (mheducation) found; the AccessEngineering URL (ISBN 9781259587542, likely 4th ed.) is search-result only and may require institutional login. Many search hits for this title are pirate PDF sites - do not use.",
  "3Blue1Brown topic pages (topics/linear-algebra, topics/calculus) load but are generic filter pages; prefer the YouTube playlists or the lessons/ URLs.",
  "Arduino docs are JS-rendered; millis() page verified by search result.",
  "Hands-On ML 3rd ed., Practical Statistics 2nd ed., Designing ML Systems: O'Reilly URLs are search-result verified.",
  "incompleteideas.net loads via HTTPS upgrade.",
  "2026-10-15: Mustafa studies on a MacBook. Setup is macOS-first (Homebrew, Xcode Command Line Tools); Linux work (apt, ROS 2) goes in an Ubuntu 26.04 arm64 VM under UTM."
 ]
}